<div style="float:left;line-height:7pt;text-align:left;width:2.88pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:5pt;position:relative;top:0;">1</font></div>
<div style="float:left;line-height:10.0pt;margin-left:7.12pt;text-align:left;width:245.00pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">&#8220;Other Expenses&#8221; reflect estimated expenses for the Fund's first fiscal
year.</font></div> </div> <div style="clear:both;position:relative;"> </div> </div> <div> <div style="clear:both;margin-top:2.0pt;position:relative;width:100%;"> <div style="float:left;line-height:7pt;text-align:left;width:2.88pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:5pt;position:relative;top:0;">2</font></div> <div style="float:left;line-height:10.0pt;margin-left:7.12pt;text-align:left;width:245.00pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">Pacific Investment Management Company LLC (&#8220;PIMCO&#8221;) has contractually agreed, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">through </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">October 31, 2027</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">, to waive its management fee, or reimburse the Fund, to the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">extent that organizational expenses, pro rata share of expenses related to obtaining or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">maintaining a Legal
Entity Identifier and pro rata Trustees&#8217; fees exceed 0.0049% of the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">Fund&#8217;s average net assets (the &#8220;Expense Limit&#8221;). Under the Expense Limitation
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">Agreement, which renews annually for a full year unless terminated by PIMCO upon at </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">least 30
days&#8217; notice prior to the end of the contract term, PIMCO may recoup these </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">waivers and reimbursements in future periods, not exceeding three years, provided that
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">organizational expenses, pro rata share of expenses related to obtaining or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">maintaining a Legal
Entity Identifier and pro rata Trustees&#8217; fees, plus recoupment, do </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">not exceed the Expense Limit (or the amount of the expense limit in place at the time </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;">the amount being recouped was originally waived if lower than the Expense Limit).</font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:10pt;"> </font></div>
</div> <div style="clear:both;position:relative;"> </div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6.0pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Example.</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Example is intended to help you compare the cost of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investing in the Fund with the costs of investing in
other </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exchange-traded funds. The Example assumes that you invest $10,000 </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">in the Fund for the time
periods indicated, and then hold or&nbsp;sell all of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">your shares at the end of those periods. The Example also assumes that </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">your investment has a 5% return each year and that the Fund&#8217;s </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">operating expenses remain the same.
Although your actual costs may be </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">higher or lower, based on these assumptions your costs would
be:</font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:1pt;">&#8195;</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:0.0pt;margin-top:6.0pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="margin-top:0.0pt;">
<table style="border-bottom:0.5pt solid #00687D;empty-cells:show;width:260pt;" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
<tr style="height:8.5pt;">
<td style="background-color:#FFFFFF;border-right:0.5pt solid #FFFFFF;padding-bottom:3.5pt;padding-top:3.5pt;vertical-align:Bottom;width:130pt;"> <div style="line-height:7pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-left:3pt;margin-right:5.75pt;text-align:Center;white-space:nowrap;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:7pt;font-weight:bold;">1 Year</font></div> </div> </td>
<td style="background-color:#FFFFFF;padding-bottom:3.5pt;padding-top:3.5pt;vertical-align:Bottom;width:130pt;"> <div style="line-height:7pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-left:5.75pt;margin-right:3pt;text-align:Center;white-space:nowrap;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:7pt;font-weight:bold;">3 Years</font></div> </div> </td> </tr>
<tr style="height:9pt;">
<td style="background-color:azure;border-right:0.5pt solid #FFFFFF;padding-bottom:2.5pt;padding-top:3.5pt;vertical-align:Top;width:130pt;"> <div style="line-height:7.5pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-left:3pt;margin-right:5.75pt;text-align:Center;white-space:nowrap;"><font style="color:#3F3F3F;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:7.5pt;margin-left:0.0pt;">$26</font></div> </div> </td>
<td style="background-color:azure;padding-bottom:2.5pt;padding-top:3.5pt;vertical-align:Top;width:130pt;"> <div style="line-height:7.5pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-left:5.75pt;margin-right:3pt;text-align:Center;white-space:nowrap;"><font
style="color:#3F3F3F;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:7.5pt;margin-left:0.0pt;">$98</font></div> </div> </td> </tr> </table> </div> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Portfolio Turnover</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund pays transaction costs when it buys and sells securities (or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">&#8220;turns over&#8221; its portfolio).
A higher portfolio turnover rate may indicate </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">higher transaction costs and may result in higher taxes when Fund </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">shares are held in a taxable account. These costs, which are not </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">reflected in the Annual Fund Operating
Expenses or in the Example </font></div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:18pt;margin-top:2.2pt;width:264pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">tables, affect the Fund&#8217;s performance. The Fund had not yet commenced </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">operations as of the most recent
fiscal year end. Thus, no portfolio </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">turnover rate is provided for the Fund.</font></div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Principal Investment Strategies</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund seeks to achieve its investment objective by, investing under
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">normal circumstances, at least 80% of its net assets in inflation-indexed </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">bonds of varying
maturities issued by the U.S. and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">non-U.S. governments, their agencies or instrumentalities, and
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">corporations, which may be represented by forwards or derivatives such </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">as options, futures
contracts or swap agreements. Inflation-linked bonds </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">are fixed income securities that are structured to provide protection </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">against inflation. The Fund intends to complement this exposure with </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investments in inflation-related
derivatives and/or other inflation-related </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">transactions, such as those tied to inflation-linked bonds (which may </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">include swaps on inflation-indexed bonds) or the Consumer Price Index </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">(CPI) (which may include swaps and
options), the inflation measure for </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">U.S. Treasury Inflation-Protected Securities (&#8220;TIPS&#8221;), in an effort to seek </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">to mitigate the effects of inflation and to benefit from inflation surprises </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">(when realized inflation exceeds
expected inflation). The Fund intends to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">use these instruments and/or transactions to allow the Fund to pursue a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">more capital efficient inflation hedge relative to a portfolio of only direct </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investments in inflation-indexed
bonds (subject to transaction, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">derivative and Fund operating expenses). &#8220;Capital efficient&#8221; refers to </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund&#8217;s ability to obtain inflation exposure on a notional basis </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">through inflation-related
derivatives and/or other inflation related </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">transactions rather than fully funding such exposure through direct </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investments of inflation-indexed bonds. Such investments will be </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">actively managed by PIMCO, which will also
adjust the level of exposure </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">to these trades based on its market expectations. The Fund&#8217;s notional </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exposure to inflation-related derivatives and/or other inflation-related </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">transactions may, and generally is
expected to, equal or exceed the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund&#8217;s net assets. As used in the investment objective, &#8220;real return&#8221; </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">equals total return less the estimated cost of inflation, which is typically </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">measured by the change in an
official inflation measure.</font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund may also invest in other securities issued by the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">U.S. Government, its agencies or
government-sponsored entities, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">derivatives and repurchase agreements related thereto (such as
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">U.S. Treasury futures and interest rate swaps), and/or interest rate </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">futures. The Fund may also
engage in financing transactions, such as </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">reverse repurchase agreements and/or total return swaps.</font><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund will normally limit its net foreign currency exposure (from </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">non-U.S. currencies) to 20% of its total
assets. The average portfolio </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">duration of this Fund normally varies within (negative) 2 years to
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">positive 2 years of the portfolio duration of the securities comprising the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">ICE U.S. Treasury 0-1
Year Inflation Linked Bond Index as calculated by </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">PIMCO, which, as of January 30, 2026, was 0.61 years. Duration is a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">measure used to determine the sensitivity of a security&#8217;s price to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">changes in interest rates. The longer
a security&#8217;s duration, the more </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">sensitive it will be to changes in interest rates.</font><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;">
<div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:right;"> <hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">PIMCO ETF Trust | </font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">Prospectus</font><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">&#8194;&#8194;</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">1</font></div> <div style="clear:both;">
</div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-12pt;position:relative;width:538pt;z-index:-1;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="margin-top:0.00pt;text-align:left;">
<img src="g133485imgabc8156a3.gif" alt=" " style="height:10pt;width:79pt;"><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:13.03pt;line-height:1pt;">&#8201;</font></div> </div> </div> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div> <hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_eef65092-f261-4bef-aa21-1b0e70cc3e83_2"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:30pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">PIMCO Inflation PLUS
Active Exchange-Traded Fund</font></div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:55.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:46.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-12pt;width:264pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund may invest only in investment
grade securities of issuers that </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">are rated at least Baa by Moody&#8217;s Ratings (&#8220;Moody&#8217;s&#8221;), or equivalently </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">rated by Standard &amp; Poor&#8217;s Ratings Services (&#8220;S&amp;P&#8221;) or Fitch Ratings, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Inc.
(&#8220;Fitch&#8221;), or if unrated, determined by PIMCO to be of comparable </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">quality. In the event that ratings services assign different ratings to the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">same security, PIMCO will use the highest rating as the credit rating for </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">that security.</font><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund may invest, without limitation, in derivative instruments, such </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">as options, futures contracts or swap
agreements, subject to applicable </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">law and any other restrictions described in the Fund&#8217;s prospectus or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Statement of Additional Information. The Fund may purchase or sell </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities on a when-issued, delayed
delivery or forward commitment </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">basis and may engage in short sales. The Fund may, without limitation, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">seek to obtain market exposure to the securities in which it primarily </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">invests by entering into a series of
purchase and sale contracts or by </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">using other investment techniques (such as buy backs or dollar rolls).</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Principal Risks</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">It is possible to lose money on an investment in the Fund.</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> The principal </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">risks of investing in the Fund, which could adversely affect its net asset </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">value, yield and total return, are&nbsp;listed below:</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Inflation Hedging Strategy Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that an inflation-hedging </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">strategy may be unsuccessful and may not protect against inflation as
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">intended. If realized inflation is lower than expected or market-implied </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inflation at the time
positions are established, the Fund may incur </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">losses. The Fund may also underperform other inflation-linked strategies </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or indices during certain interest rate environments, including during </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">periods of declining yields. Inflation
hedging strategies also involve </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">costs, including premiums, financing, transaction, roll costs, and other </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">derivative-related expenses that may negatively impact performance</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Inflation-Indexed Security Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that inflation-indexed debt </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities are subject to the effects of actual or anticipated changes in
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">market interest rates caused by factors other than inflation (real interest </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">rates). In general,
the value of an inflation-indexed security, including </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">TIPS, tends to decrease when real interest rates increase and can </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">increase when real interest rates decrease. Interest payments on </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inflation-indexed securities are
unpredictable and will fluctuate as the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">principal and interest are adjusted based on the rate of inflation. There </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">can be no assurance that the inflation index used will accurately </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">measure the real rate of inflation in the
prices of goods and services. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Any increase in the principal amount of an inflation-indexed debt
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">security will be considered taxable ordinary income, even though the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund will not receive the
principal until maturity</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">New Fund Risk:</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that a new fund&#8217;s performance may not </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">represent how the fund is expected to or may perform in the long term. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">In addition, new funds have limited
operating histories for investors to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">evaluate and new funds may not attract sufficient assets to achieve </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investment and trading efficiencies</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Small Fund Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that a smaller fund may not achieve </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investment or trading efficiencies or may be limited in ability
to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">participate in certain investment opportunities due to its size. </font></div> </div> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:18pt;margin-top:-12pt;width:264pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Additionally, a smaller fund may be more
adversely affected by large </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">purchases or redemptions by investors</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Market Trading Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that an active secondary trading market </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">for Fund shares does not continue once developed, that the
Fund may </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">not continue to meet a listing exchange&#8217;s trading or listing </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">requirements, that
trading in Fund shares may be halted or become less </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">liquid, or that Fund shares trade at prices other than the Fund&#8217;s net </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">asset value and are subject to trading costs. These risks may be </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exacerbated if the creation/redemption
process becomes less effective, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">particularly during times of market stress or volatility</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Interest Rate Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that fixed income securities will fluctuate </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">in value due to changes in interest rates; a fund with a
longer average </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">portfolio duration will be more sensitive to changes in interest rates </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">than a fund
with a shorter average portfolio duration. Factors such as </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">government policy, inflation, the economy, and market for bonds can </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">impact interest rates and yields</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Call Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that an issuer may exercise its right to redeem a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">fixed income security earlier than expected (a
call). Issuers may call </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">outstanding securities prior to their maturity for a number of reasons
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">including declining interest rates, changes in credit spreads and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">improvements in the
issuer&#8217;s credit quality. If an issuer calls a security </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">that the Fund has invested in, the Fund may not recoup the full amount </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">of its initial investment or may not realize the full anticipated earnings </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">from the investment and may be
forced to reinvest in lower-yielding </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities, securities with greater credit risks or securities with other, less </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">favorable features</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Credit Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that the Fund could experience losses if the issuer </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or guarantor of a fixed income security, the
counterparty to a derivative </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">contract, or the issuer or guarantor of collateral, is unable or unwilling, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or is perceived (whether by market participants, rating agencies, pricing </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">services or otherwise) as unable or
unwilling, to meet its financial </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">obligations</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Market Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that the value of securities owned by the Fund </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">may fluctuate, sometimes rapidly or unpredictably, due
to a variety of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">factors affecting securities markets generally or particular industries or
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">sectors</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Issuer Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that the value of a security may decline for reasons </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">related to the issuer, such as management
performance, changes in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">financial condition or credit rating, financial leverage, reputation or
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">reduced demand for the issuer&#8217;s goods or services</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Liquidity Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that a particular investment may be difficult to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">purchase or sell and that the Fund may be unable to
sell investments at </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">an advantageous time or price or achieve its desired level of exposure to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">a
certain sector. Liquidity risk may result from the lack of an active </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">market, reduced number and capacity of traditional market participants </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">to make a market in fixed income securities, and may be magnified in a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">rising interest rate environment or
other circumstances where investor </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">redemptions from fixed income funds may be higher than normal,
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">causing increased supply in the market due to selling activity. The </font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">2&#8194;&#8194;Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;"> | PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div> <hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_eef65092-f261-4bef-aa21-1b0e70cc3e83_3"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:30pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">Prospectus</font></div>
</div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:55.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:46.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-12pt;width:264pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">liquidity of the Fund&#8217;s shares may
be constrained by the liquidity of the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund&#8217;s portfolio holdings</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Derivatives Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk of investing in derivative instruments (such </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">as forwards, futures, options, swaps and structured
securities) and other </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">similar investments, including leverage, liquidity, interest rate, market,
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">counterparty (including credit), operational, legal and management </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">risks, and valuation
complexity. Changes in the value of a derivative or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">other similar investment may not correlate perfectly with, and may be </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">more sensitive to market events than, the underlying asset, rate or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">index, and the Fund could lose more than
the initial amount invested. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Changes in the value of a derivative or other similar instrument may
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">also create margin delivery or settlement payment obligations for the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund. The Fund&#8217;s use
of derivatives or other similar investments may </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">result in losses to the Fund, a reduction in the Fund&#8217;s returns and/or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">increased volatility. Non-centrally-cleared over-the-counter (&#8220;OTC&#8221;) </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">derivatives or other similar
investments are also subject to the risk that </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">a counterparty to the transaction will not fulfill its contractual </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">obligations to the other party, as many of the protections afforded to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">centrally-cleared derivative
transactions might not be available for </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">non-centrally cleared OTC derivatives or other similar investments. The </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">primary credit risk on derivatives or other similar investments that are </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exchange-traded or traded through a
central clearing counterparty </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">resides with the Fund's clearing broker or the clearinghouse. Changes in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">regulations relating to a registered fund&#8217;s use of derivatives and related </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">instruments could potentially
limit or impact the Fund&#8217;s ability to invest </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">in derivatives, limit the Fund&#8217;s ability to employ certain strategies that </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">use derivatives or other similar investments and/or adversely affect the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">value of derivatives or other similar
investments and the Fund&#8217;s </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">performance</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Exchange-Traded Fund Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that an exchange-traded fund </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">may not achieve its investment objective, among other reasons, because
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">of regulatory restrictions, including, for example, exchange rules, market </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">prices of shares of an
exchange-traded fund may fluctuate rapidly and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">materially, or shares of an exchange-traded fund may trade significantly </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">above or below net asset value, any of which may cause losses to the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund invested in the exchange-traded
fund</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Foreign (Non-U.S.) Investment Risk:</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that investing in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">foreign (non-U.S.) securities may result in the Fund experiencing more </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">rapid and extreme changes in value than
a fund that invests exclusively </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">in securities of U.S. companies, due to smaller or less developed
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">markets, differing financial reporting, accounting, corporate governance </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and auditing standards,
increased risk of delayed settlement of portfolio </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">transactions or loss of certificates of portfolio securities, and the risk of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">unfavorable U.S. or foreign government actions, including </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">nationalization, expropriation or confiscatory
taxation, currency </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">blockage, political changes, diplomatic developments, trade restrictions
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">(including tariffs) or the imposition of sanctions and other similar </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">measures. Foreign securities
may also be less liquid and more difficult to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">value than securities of U.S. issuers</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Sovereign Debt Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that investments in fixed income </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">instruments issued by sovereign entities may decline in value as a
result </font></div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:18pt;margin-top:-12pt;width:264pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">of
default or other adverse credit events resulting from an issuer&#8217;s </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inability or unwillingness to make principal or interest payments in a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">timely fashion</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Currency Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that foreign (non-U.S.) currencies may </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">fluctuate in value relative to the U.S. dollar, which can
affect the value of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund&#8217;s investments in foreign (non-U.S.) currencies or in securities
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">that trade in, and receive revenues in, or in derivatives that provide </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exposure to, foreign
(non-U.S.) currencies</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Leveraging Risk:</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that certain transactions of the Fund, such </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">as reverse repurchase agreements, loans of portfolio securities, and the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">use of when-issued, delayed delivery
or forward commitment </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">transactions, and derivative instruments may give rise to leverage,
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">magnifying gains and losses and causing the Fund to be more volatile </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">than if it had not been
leveraged. This means that leverage entails a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">heightened risk of loss. The use of leverage may also increase the Fund&#8217;s </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">sensitivity to interest rate changes and other market risks</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Management Risk:</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk that the investment techniques and risk </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">analyses applied by PIMCO will not produce the desired
results and that </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">actual or potential conflicts of interest, legislative, regulatory, or tax
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">restrictions, policies or developments may affect the investment </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">techniques available to PIMCO
and the individual portfolio managers in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">connection with managing the Fund and may cause PIMCO to restrict or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">prohibit participation in certain investments. There is no guarantee that </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the investment objective of the Fund
will be achieved</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:6pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Short Exposure Risk:</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;">&#8201;</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk of entering into short sales or other </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">short positions, including the potential loss of more money than the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">actual cost of the investment, and the
risk that the third party to the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">short sale or other short position will not fulfill its contractual </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">obligations, causing a loss to the Fund</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Please see &#8220;Description of Principal Risks&#8221; in the Fund's prospectus for </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">a more detailed
description of the risks of investing in the Fund. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">An </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investment in the Fund is not a deposit of
a bank and is not insured or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">guaranteed by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation or any other
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">government agency.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:9pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:9pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Investment Adviser/Portfolio Managers</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:2pt;text-align:left;min-height:72pt;">
<img src="g133485cudzil_mike.jpg" alt=" " style="float:left;height:72pt;width:48pt;margin-right:5pt;">
<img src="g133485he_daniel.jpg" alt=" " style="float:left;height:72pt;width:48pt;margin-right:5pt;">
<img src="g133485dora_tanuj.jpg" alt=" " style="float:left;height:72pt;width:48pt;margin-right:5pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">PIMCO serves as the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investment manager for </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund. The Fund&#8217;s </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">portfolio is jointly and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">primarily managed by </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Mike Cudzil, Daniel He </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and Tanuj Dora. Mr. Cudzil is a Managing Director of PIMCO. Mr. He is </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">an Executive Vice President of PIMCO. Mr. Dora is a Senior Vice </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">President of PIMCO. Messrs. Cudzil, He and
Dora have managed the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund since its inception.</font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:right;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">February 21, 2026 &nbsp;(as supplemented March 31, 2026) | </font><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">&#8194;&#8194;</font><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">3</font></div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div>
<hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_eef65092-f261-4bef-aa21-1b0e70cc3e83_4"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:30pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">PIMCO Inflation PLUS
Active Exchange-Traded Fund</font></div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:55.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:46.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-12pt;width:264pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Performance
Information</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund does not have a full calendar year of performance.
Thus, no </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">bar chart or Average Annual Total Returns table is included for the Fund. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Once the Fund
commences operations, performance for the Fund will be </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">updated daily and quarterly and may be obtained as follows: daily and </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">quarterly updates on the net asset value and performance page at
</font><font style="color:#3333FF;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">https://www.pimco.com/us/en/product-finder?filters=products=etf</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">.</font><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Purchase and Sale of Fund Shares</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund is an exchange-traded fund (&#8220;ETF&#8221;). Individual Fund shares </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">may only be purchased and sold
on a national securities exchange </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">through a broker-dealer and may not be purchased or redeemed directly </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">with the Fund.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The price of Fund shares is based on market price, and because ETF </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">shares trade at market prices rather than
net asset value (&#8220;NAV&#8221;), </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">shares may trade at a price greater than NAV (a premium) or less than </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">NAV (a discount). An investor may incur costs attributable to the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">difference between the highest price a buyer
is willing to pay to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">purchase shares of the Fund (&#8220;bid&#8221;) and the lowest price a seller is </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">willing to accept for shares (&#8220;ask&#8221;) when buying or selling shares in the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">secondary market (the
&#8220;bid-ask spread&#8221;). Recent information, including </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">information about the Fund&#8217;s NAV, market price, premiums and </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">discounts, and bid-ask spreads, is included on the Fund&#8217;s website at
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">https://www.pimco.com/en-us/investments/etf.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Tax Information</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund's distributions are generally taxable to you as ordinary income, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">capital gains, or a combination of
the two, unless you are investing </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">through a tax-deferred arrangement, such as a 401(k) plan or an
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">individual retirement account, in which case distributions may be </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">taxable upon
withdrawal.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Payments to Broker-Dealers and
Other Financial </font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Intermediaries</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">If you purchase Fund shares through a broker-dealer or other financial </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">intermediary, PIMCO or other related
companies may pay the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">intermediary for the sale of Fund shares or related services. These
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">payments may create a conflict of interest by influencing the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">broker-dealer or other intermediary
and your salesperson to recommend </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund over another investment. Ask your salesperson or visit your </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">financial intermediary&#8217;s website for more information.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Summary Information About the Fund</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:2pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">This prospectus describes the PIMCO Inflation PLUS Active </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Exchange-Traded Fund (the &#8220;Fund&#8221;)
offered by PIMCO ETF Trust (the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">&#8220;Trust&#8221;). The Fund provides access to the professional investment </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">advisory services offered by PIMCO.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">ETFs are funds that trade like other publicly-traded securities and may </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">be designed to track an index or to be
actively managed. Unlike </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">conventional ETFs, the Fund is not an index fund. The Fund is actively
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">managed and does not seek to replicate the performance of a specified </font></div> </div> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:18pt;margin-top:-12pt;width:264pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">index. Unlike shares of a mutual fund,
which can be bought from and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">redeemed by the issuing fund by all shareholders at a price based on
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">NAV, shares of the Fund may be directly purchased from and redeemed </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">by the Fund at NAV solely by
a member or participant of a clearing </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">agency registered with the Securities and Exchange Commission, which </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">has a written agreement with the Fund&#8217;s Distributor that allows such </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">member or participant to place
orders for the purchase and redemption </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">of Creation Units (as defined below) (&#8220;Authorized Participant&#8220;). Also </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">unlike shares of a mutual fund, shares of the Fund are listed on a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">national securities exchange and trade in
the secondary market at </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">market prices that change throughout the day.</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Once operational, shares of the Fund are listed and traded at market </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">prices
on Nasdaq Stock Market (&#8220;Nasdaq&#8221;) and other secondary </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">markets. The market price for the Fund&#8217;s shares may be different from </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund&#8217;s NAV. The Fund issues and redeems shares at NAV only in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">aggregations of a specified number of
shares (&#8221;Creation Units&#8220;). Only </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Authorized Participants may purchase or redeem Creation Units directly </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">with the Fund at NAV. These transactions are in exchange for securities </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and/or cash. Except when aggregated in
Creation Units, shares of the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund are not redeemable securities. Shareholders who are not
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Authorized Participants may not purchase or redeem shares directly </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">from the Fund.</font></div>
</div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">If the Fund were to effect redemptions with an Authorized Participant </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">primarily for cash, the Fund may be required to sell portfolio securities in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">order to obtain the cash needed
to distribute redemption proceeds. The </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">sale of portfolio securities could cause the Fund to recognize gains that </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">it might not otherwise have recognized if redemptions were effected </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">in-kind, or to recognize such gain sooner
than would otherwise be </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">required. Such gains will generally be distributed to shareholders to
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">avoid taxation at the Fund level and to ensure compliance with other </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">special tax rules that apply
to the Fund. Moreover, the sale of portfolio </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities will generally subject the Fund to transaction costs, which may </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">be partially or totally offset by the variable transaction fee charged by </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund to redeeming Authorized
Participants.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">An investment in the Fund alone should not
constitute an entire </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investment program. This prospectus explains what you should know </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">about the
Fund before you invest. Please read it carefully. Certain </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">affiliates of the Fund and PIMCO may purchase and resell Fund shares </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">pursuant to this prospectus.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">On each business day, before commencement of trading on Nasdaq, the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund will disclose on www.pimcoetfs.com
the identities and quantities </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">of the Fund&#8217;s portfolio holdings that will form the basis for the Fund&#8217;s </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">calculation of NAV at the end of the business day. The Fund fact sheet </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">provides additional information
regarding the Fund and may be </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">requested by calling 1.888.400.4ETF (1.888.400.4383).</font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">4&#8194;&#8194;Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;"> | PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div> <hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_c860aaf9-7e50-4176-bbd5-2fbb95d53c49_1"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">Prospectus</font></div>
</div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Description of Principal
Risks</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:2pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The value of your investment in the Fund changes with the market
price of the Fund&#8217;s shares determined in the secondary market. Market price may </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">be determined, in part, by the values of the Fund&#8217;s investments. Many factors can
affect those values. The factors that are most likely to have a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">material effect on the Fund&#8217;s portfolio as a whole are called &#8220;principal risks.&#8221; The
principal risks of the Fund are identified in the Fund Summary and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">are described in this section. The Fund may be subject to additional risks other than those identified and
described below because the types of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investments made by the Fund can change over time. Securities and investment techniques mentioned in this summary that appear in bold
type are </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">described in greater detail under &#8220;Characteristics and Risks of Securities and Investment Techniques.&#8221; That section and &#8220;Investment Objectives and
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Policies&#8221; in the Statement of Additional Information (&#8220;SAI&#8221;) also include more information about the Fund, its investments and the related risks. There
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">is no guarantee that the Fund will be able to achieve its investment objective. It is possible to lose money by investing in the Fund.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Inflation Hedging Strategy Risk</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Inflation hedging strategies typically involve investments in assets that are
historically considered to be responsive to inflationary pressures, such as </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">commodities, real assets, inflation-protected securities, or other inflation-focused instruments.
These assets may underperform during periods of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">disinflation, deflation, or economic instability, and their value can be adversely affected by general market conditions,
supply-demand dynamics, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">geopolitical events, or other macroeconomic factors unrelated to inflation. Inflation rates are influenced by complex economic factors that are not
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">always predictable or consistent with historical norms. There is no guarantee that the selected hedging instruments will effectively offset inflationary </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">risks, particularly if inflation is driven by atypical or unforeseen circumstances. Additionally, central bank interventions, fiscal policies, or structural </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">economic changes may cause inflation to deviate significantly from projections, which could impair the effectiveness of the Fund&#8217;s strategy.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Hedging strategies designed to mitigate inflation risk may not accomplish their
intended objectives if they are improperly managed, based on </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inaccurate assumptions about inflation trends or if realized inflation is lower than anticipated. The use of
derivative instruments, leverage, or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">concentrated investments in inflation-sensitive assets introduces additional layers of risk, including, but not limited to, liquidity
risk, counterparty risk, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and heightened exposure to market volatility. Certain inflation-focused investments, such as commodities or alternative assets, may be less liquid
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">than traditional securities. Difficulty in liquidating positions at favorable prices may result in losses or reduced returns, particularly during times of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">economic stress or market disruption. While inflation hedging instruments are designed to mitigate inflation-specific risks, they may fail to perform as </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">expected due to insufficient correlation between the asset and inflation trends. Historical correlations are not guaranteed to persist under changing </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">economic conditions, and investors may face unexpected losses if the hedging strategy relies on outdated or inaccurate assumptions. Inflation </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">hedging strategies often incur additional costs, including transaction fees, management fees, and derivative-related expenses, which may negatively </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">affect returns. High costs can negate inflation-risk mitigation benefits, particularly in periods of low or moderate inflation. During periods of stable or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">declining inflation or when inflation fails to materialize as anticipated, inflation-sensitive assets or strategies may underperform compared to </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">traditional investments. In such instances, investors may forfeit opportunities for better returns in other asset classes. The Fund may also underperform </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">other inflation-linked strategies or indices during certain interest rate environments, including during periods of declining yields.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Inflation-Indexed Security Risk</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Inflation-indexed debt securities are subject to the effects of actual or anticipated
changes in market interest rates caused by factors other than </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inflation (real interest rates). In general, the value of an inflation-indexed security, including TIPS, tends
to decrease when real interest rates increase </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and can increase when real interest rates decrease. Thus generally, during periods of rising inflation, the value of
inflation-indexed securities will tend </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">to increase and during periods of deflation, their value will tend to decrease. Interest payments on inflation-indexed securities can
be unpredictable </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and will fluctuate as the principal and/or interest are adjusted based on the rate of inflation. There can be no assurance that the inflation index used
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">(i.e., the CPI), which is calculated and published by a third party, will accurately measure the real rate of inflation in the prices of goods and services. </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Increases in the principal value of TIPS due to inflation are considered taxable ordinary income for the amount of the increase in the calendar year. </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Any increase in the principal amount of an inflation-indexed debt security will be considered taxable ordinary income, even though the Fund will not </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">receive the principal until maturity. As a result, a Fund may be required to make distributions to shareholders that exceed the cash the Fund received, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">which may cause the Fund to liquidate certain investments when it is not advantageous to do so. Also, if the principal value of an inflation-indexed </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">security is adjusted downward due to deflation, amounts previously distributed may be characterized in some circumstances as a return of capital.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Additionally, a CPI swap can potentially lose value if the realized rate of inflation
over the life of the swap is less than the fixed market implied </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inflation rate (fixed breakeven rate) that the investor agrees to pay at the initiation of the swap. With
municipal inflation-indexed securities, the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inflation adjustment is integrated into the coupon payment, which is federally tax exempt (and may be state tax exempt). For
municipal </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inflation-indexed securities, there is no adjustment to the principal value. Because municipal inflation-indexed securities are a small component of the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">municipal bond market, they may be less liquid than conventional municipal bonds.</font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:right;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">February 21, 2026&nbsp;(as supplemented March 31, 2026) |
</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">&#8194;&#8194;</font><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">5</font></div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div>
<hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_c860aaf9-7e50-4176-bbd5-2fbb95d53c49_2"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">New Fund
Risk</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">A new Fund&#8217;s performance may not represent how the Fund is
expected to or may perform in the long term if and when it becomes larger and has </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">fully implemented its investment strategies. Investment positions may have a
disproportionate impact (negative or positive) on performance in new </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Funds. New Funds may also require a period of time before they are fully invested in securities that
meet their investment objectives and policies and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">achieve a representative portfolio composition. Fund performance may be lower or higher during this &#8220;ramp-up&#8221;
period, and may also be more </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">volatile, than would be the case after the Fund is fully invested. Similarly, a new Fund&#8217;s investment strategy may require a longer period
of time to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">show returns that are representative of the strategy. New Funds have limited performance histories for investors to evaluate and new Funds may not </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">attract sufficient assets to achieve investment and trading efficiencies. If a new Fund were to fail to successfully implement its investment strategies or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">achieve its investment objective, performance may be negatively impacted, and any resulting liquidation could create negative transaction costs for </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund and tax consequences for investors.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Small Fund Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">A smaller fund may not grow to or maintain an economically viable size to achieve investment or trading efficiencies or may be limited in ability to </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">participate in certain investment opportunities due to its size, which may negatively impact performance and/or force the fund to liquidate. </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Additionally, a smaller fund may be more adversely affected by large purchases or redemptions by investors, which can occur at any time and may </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">impact the fund in the same manner as a high volume of purchases or redemptions.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Market Trading Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund is subject to secondary market trading risks. Shares of the Fund are listed for trading on an exchange, however, there can be no guarantee
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">that an active trading market for such shares will develop or continue. Shares of the Fund may be listed or traded on U.S. and foreign (non-U.S.) </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exchanges other than the Fund&#8217;s primary U.S. listing exchange. There can be no guarantee that the Fund&#8217;s shares will continue trading on any </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exchange or in any market or that the Fund&#8217;s shares will continue to meet the listing or trading requirements of any exchange or market. The Fund&#8217;s </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">shares may experience higher trading volumes on one exchange as compared to another and investors are subject to the execution and settlement </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">risks of the market where their broker directs trades.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Secondary market trading in the Fund&#8217;s shares may be halted by an exchange because of market conditions. Pursuant to exchange or market rules, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">trading in the Fund&#8217;s shares on an exchange or in any market may be subject to trading halts caused by extraordinary market volatility. If secondary </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">market trading is halted or an exchange closes earlier than anticipated, it may be impossible to purchase or sell Fund shares. Additionally, the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">secondary market for trading an exchange-traded fund&#8217;s shares may become less liquid in stressed market conditions and when the underlying </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">holdings of the exchange-traded fund are difficult to buy or sell. There can be no guarantee that the Fund&#8217;s exchange listing or ability to trade its </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">shares will continue or remain unchanged. In the event the Fund ceases to be listed on an exchange, the Fund may cease operating as an </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">&#8220;exchange-traded&#8221; fund and operate as a mutual fund, provided that shareholders are given advance notice.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Buying or selling the Fund&#8217;s shares on an exchange may require the payment of
brokerage commissions. The commission is frequently a fixed amount </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and may be a significant cost for investors seeking to buy or sell small amounts of shares. In addition,
an investor who buys or sells may also incur the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">cost of the spread (the difference between the bid price and the ask price). The spread varies over time for shares of the
Fund based on their trading </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">volume and market liquidity and is generally less if the Fund has more trading volume and market liquidity and more if the Fund has less trading
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">volume and market liquidity. Due to the costs inherent in buying or selling the Fund&#8217;s shares, frequent trading may detract significantly from </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investment returns. Investment in the Fund&#8217;s shares may not be advisable for investors who expect to engage in frequent trading.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Shares of the Fund may trade on an exchange at prices at, above or below their most
recent NAV, which could result in an investor buying shares of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund at a higher price than the Fund's NAV or selling shares of the Fund at a lower price than the Fund's
NAV. The market prices of Fund shares </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">will fluctuate, sometimes rapidly and materially, in response to the Fund's changes in the Fund&#8217;s NAV, the value of Fund holdings
and supply and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">demand for Fund shares. Although the creation/redemption feature of the Fund generally makes it more likely that Fund shares will trade close to </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">NAV, market volatility, lack of an active trading market for Fund shares, disruptions at market participants (such as Authorized Participants or market </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">makers) and any disruptions in the ordinary functioning of the creation/redemption process may result in Fund shares trading significantly above (at a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">&#8220;premium&#8221;) or below (at a &#8220;discount&#8221;) NAV. Additionally, to the extent the Fund holds securities traded in markets that close at a different time from </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund&#8217;s listing exchange, liquidity in such securities may be reduced after the applicable closing times, and during the time when the Fund&#8217;s listing </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exchange is open but after the applicable market closing, fixing or settlement times, bid/ask spreads and the resulting premium or discount to the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund&#8217;s shares&#8217; NAV may widen. Selling shares may be difficult or may result in significant losses if transactions in Fund shares occur under these and </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">other circumstances. Neither PIMCO nor the Trust can predict whether Fund shares will trade above, below or at NAV. The Fund&#8217;s investment results </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">are based on the Fund&#8217;s daily NAV. Investors transacting in Fund shares in the secondary market, where market prices may differ from NAV, may </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">experience investment results that differ from results based on the Fund&#8217;s daily NAV. There are various methods by which investors can purchase and </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">sell shares and various orders that may be placed. Investors should consult their financial intermediary before purchasing or selling shares of the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund.</font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;">
<div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;"> <hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">6&#8194;&#8194;Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;"> | PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div> <hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_c860aaf9-7e50-4176-bbd5-2fbb95d53c49_3"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">Prospectus</font></div>
</div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund has a limited number of
intermediaries that act as Authorized Participants, and none of these Authorized Participants are or will be </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">obligated to engage in creation or redemption transactions. To
the extent that these intermediaries exit the business or are unable to or choose not to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">proceed with creation and/or redemption orders with respect to the Fund and no other
Authorized Participant is able and willing to create or redeem, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">shares may trade at a discount to NAV and possibly face trading halts and/ or delisting. Additionally, while
Fund shares are listed for trading on an </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exchange, there can be no assurance that active trading markets for Fund shares will be maintained by market makers or Authorized
Participants.</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Decisions by market makers or Authorized Participants to
reduce their role or &#8220;step away&#8221; from these activities in times of market stress or volatility </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">may inhibit the effectiveness of the creation/redemption process
in maintaining the relationship between the underlying value of the Fund&#8217;s holdings </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and the Fund&#8217;s NAV. Such reduced effectiveness could result in the
Fund&#8217;s shares trading at a discount to its NAV and also in greater than normal </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">intraday bid/ask spreads for the Fund&#8217;s shares.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Interest Rate Risk</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Interest rate risk is the risk that </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">fixed income securities</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> and other instruments in the Fund&#8217;s portfolio will fluctuate in
value due to changes, or the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">anticipation of changes, in interest rates. Factors including central bank monetary policy, rising inflation rates, and changes in general
economic </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">conditions may cause interest rates to rise, which could cause the value of the Fund&#8217;s investments to decline. For example, as nominal interest rates </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">rise, the value of certain securities held by the Fund is likely to decrease. A nominal interest rate can be described as the sum of a real interest rate and </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">an expected inflation rate. Interest rate changes can be sudden and unpredictable, and the Fund may experience losses as a result of movements in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">interest rates. The Fund may not be able to hedge against changes in interest rates or may choose not to do so for cost or other reasons. In addition, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">any hedges may not work as intended.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Fixed income securities</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> with longer durations tend to be more sensitive to changes in
interest rates, usually making them more volatile than </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities with shorter durations. The values of equity and other non-fixed income securities may also decline due to
fluctuations in interest rates. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Inflation-indexed bonds</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, including Treasury
Inflation-Protected Securities (&#8220;TIPS&#8221;), decline in value when real interest rates rise. In certain interest </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">rate environments, such as when real interest rates
are rising faster than nominal interest rates, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">inflation-indexed bonds</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may
experience greater </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">losses than other </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">fixed income securities</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> with similar durations.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Dividend-paying equity securities</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, particularly those whose market price is closely related
to their yield, may be more sensitive to changes in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">interest rates. During periods of rising interest rates, the values of such securities may decline and may result in
losses to the Fund.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Variable and floating rate
securities</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> generally are less sensitive to interest rate changes but may decline in value if their interest rates do not rise </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">as much, or as quickly, as interest rates in general. Conversely, floating rate securities will not generally increase in value if interest rates decline. </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Inverse floating rate securities may decrease in value due to changes in interest rates. Inverse floating rate securities may also exhibit greater price </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">volatility than a fixed rate obligation with similar credit quality. When the Fund holds
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">variable or floating rate securities</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, a decrease (or, in the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">case of inverse floating rate securities, an increase) in market interest rates will adversely affect the income received from such securities and the NAV </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">of the Fund&#8217;s shares.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">A wide variety of factors can cause interest rates or yields of U.S. Treasury securities (or yields of other types of bonds) to rise, including but not limited </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">to central bank monetary policies, changing inflation or real growth rates, general economic conditions, increasing bond issuances or reduced market </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">demand for low yielding investments. Risks associated with changes in interest rates are heightened under certain market conditions, such as during </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">times when the U.S. Federal Reserve (the &#8220;Federal Reserve&#8221;) raises interest rates or when such rates remain elevated following a period of historically </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">low levels. Additionally, the U.S. and other governments have increased, and are likely to continue increasing, their debt issuances, which may also </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">heighten these risks. There is the risk that the income generated by investments may not keep pace with inflation. Actions by governments and central </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">banking authorities can result in increases or decreases in interest rates. Periods of higher inflation could cause such authorities to raise interest rates, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">which may adversely affect the Fund and its investments. In addition, changes in monetary policy may exacerbate the risks associated with changing </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">interest rates. Further, in market environments where interest rates are rising, issuers may be less willing or able to make principal and interest </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">payments on fixed income investments when due.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Rising interest rates may result in periods of volatility and a decline in value of the Fund&#8217;s fixed income investments. Further, while U.S. bond markets </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">have steadily grown over the past three decades, dealer &#8220;market making&#8221; ability has remained relatively stagnant. As a result, dealer inventories of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">certain types of bonds and similar instruments, which provide a core indication of the ability of financial intermediaries to &#8220;make markets,&#8221; are at or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">near historic lows in relation to market size. Because market makers provide stability to a market through their intermediary services, the significant </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">reduction in dealer inventories could potentially lead to decreased liquidity and increased volatility in the fixed income markets. Such issues may be </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exacerbated during periods of economic uncertainty. All of these factors, collectively and/or individually, could cause the Fund to lose value.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">During periods of very low or negative interest rates, the Fund may be unable to
maintain positive returns. Certain European countries have previously </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">experienced negative interest rates on certain </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">fixed income instruments</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">. Very low or negative interest rates may magnify interest rate risk.
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Changing interest rates, including rates that fall below zero, may have unpredictable effects on markets, may result in heightened market volatility </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and may detract from the Fund&#8217;s performance to the extent the Fund is exposed to such interest rates.</font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:right;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">February 21, 2026&nbsp;(as supplemented March 31, 2026) |
</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">&#8194;&#8194;</font><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">7</font></div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div>
<hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_c860aaf9-7e50-4176-bbd5-2fbb95d53c49_4"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Measures such as average </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">duration</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may not accurately reflect the true interest rate sensitivity of the Fund. This is
especially the case if the Fund </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">consists of securities with widely varying durations. Therefore, if the Fund has an average </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">duration</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> that suggests a certain level of interest rate risk, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund may in fact be subject to greater interest rate risk than the average would suggest. This risk is greater to the extent the Fund uses leverage </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> in
connection with the management of the Fund.</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Convexity is an additional
measure used to understand a security&#8217;s or the Fund&#8216;s interest rate sensitivity. Convexity measures the rate of change of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">duration</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> in response to changes in interest rates. With respect to a security&#8217;s price, a larger convexity (positive or negative) may imply more dramatic </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">price changes in response to changing interest rates. Convexity may be positive or negative. Negative convexity implies that interest rate increases </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">result in increased </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">duration</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, and vice versa, meaning increased sensitivity in prices in response to changes in interest rates. Thus, securities with </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">negative convexity, which may include bonds with traditional call features and certain mortgage-backed securities, may experience greater losses in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">periods of rising interest rates. Accordingly, if the Fund holds such securities, the Fund may be subject to a greater risk of losses in periods of rising </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">interest rates.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Credit Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund could experience losses if the issuer or guarantor of a fixed income security (including a security purchased with securities lending </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">collateral), the counterparty to a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> contract or a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">repurchase agreement</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">borrower of portfolio securities</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, or the issuer or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">guarantor of collateral, is unable or unwilling, or is perceived (whether by market
participants, rating agencies, pricing services or otherwise) as unable </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or unwilling, to make timely principal and/or interest payments, or to otherwise honor its
obligations. The risk that such issuer, guarantor or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">counterparty is less willing or able to do so is heightened in market environments where interest rates are changing,
notably when rates are rising.</font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The downgrade of the credit rating of a security or of the issuer of a security held by the Fund may decrease its value. Securities are subject to varying </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">degrees of credit risk, which are often reflected in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">credit ratings</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">. Measures such as average credit quality may not accurately reflect the true credit </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">risk of the Fund. This is
especially the case if the Fund consists of securities with widely varying credit ratings. Therefore, if the Fund has an average </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">credit rating that suggests a certain credit
quality, the Fund may in fact be subject to greater credit risk than the average would suggest. Credit risk is </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">greater to the extent the Fund uses leverage or derivatives in
connection with the management of the Fund, which would be magnified in the event </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">that initial or variation margin is not provided by the counterparty to such transaction
(or not provided below a certain threshold amount).</font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Credit risk includes credit spread risk, which is the risk that credit spreads (i.e., the difference in yield between securities that is due to
differences in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">their actual or perceived credit quality) may increase when the market believes that investments generally have a greater risk of default. Increasing </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">credit spreads may reduce the market value of the Fund&#8217;s investments. Credit spreads often increase more for lower rated and unrated securities than </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">for investment grade securities. In addition, when credit spreads increase, reductions in market value will generally be greater for longer-maturity </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities. Further, credit spread duration (a measure of credit spread risk) can vary significantly from interest rate duration (e.g., for floating rate debt </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities, credit spread duration typically will be higher than interest rate duration). The Fund may add credit spread duration to its portfolio, for </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">example through the use of derivatives (e.g., credit default swaps), even while it has lower interest rate duration. The credit spread duration of the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund may vary, in some cases significantly, from its interest rate duration.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Market Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The market price of securities owned by the Fund may fluctuate, sometimes rapidly or unpredictably. Securities may decline in value due to variety of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">factors affecting (or perceiving to affect) securities markets generally or particular industries or sectors or issuers represented in the securities markets. </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The value of a security may decline due to general market conditions that are not specifically related to a particular company, such as real or perceived </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">adverse economic conditions, changes in the general outlook for corporate earnings, levels of public debt and deficits, changes in inflation, interest or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">currency rates, financial systems instability, adverse changes to credit markets or adverse investor sentiment generally. The value of a security may also </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">decline due to factors that affect a particular industry or industries, such as labor shortages or increased production costs and competitive conditions </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">within an industry. During a general downturn in the securities markets, multiple asset classes may decline in value simultaneously even if the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">performance of those asset classes is not otherwise historically correlated. Investments may also be negatively impacted by market disruptions and by </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">attempts by other market participants to manipulate the prices of particular investments.
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Credit ratings</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> downgrades may also negatively affect </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities held by the Fund. Even when markets perform well, there is no assurance that the investments held by the Fund will increase in value along </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">with the broader market.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">In addition, market risk includes the risk that geopolitical and other events will disrupt the economy on a national or global level. For instance, actual </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or threatened war or armed conflicts, terrorism, social unrest, recessions, supply chain disruptions, market manipulation, government defaults, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">government shutdowns, political and regulatory changes, diplomatic developments, or the imposition of sanctions and other similar measures, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">including the imposition of tariffs, or other U.S. economic policies and any related public health emergencies (such as the spread of infectious </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">diseases, pandemics and epidemics) and natural/environmental disasters or events can all negatively impact the securities markets, which could cause </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund to lose value. These events could reduce consumer demand or economic output, result in market closures, changes in interest rates, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inflation/deflation, travel restrictions or quarantines, and significantly adversely impact the economy.</font><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;">
<div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;"> <hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">8&#8194;&#8194;Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;"> | PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div> <hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_c860aaf9-7e50-4176-bbd5-2fbb95d53c49_5"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">Prospectus</font></div>
</div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">As computing technology and data analytics
advance, there has been a trend towards machine driven and artificially intelligent trading systems, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">particularly with respect to increasing levels of autonomy in trading
decision capabilities. Regulators of financial markets have become increasingly </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">focused on the potential impact of artificial intelligence on investment activities and may
issue regulations that affect the use of artificial technology </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">in trading activities. Any such regulations may not have the effect on financial markets that regulators
intend. Moreover, advancements in artificial </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">intelligence and other technologies may result in the introduction of errors, defects or security vulnerabilities, which can go
undetected. The potential </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">speed of such trading and other technologies may exacerbate the impact of any such incidents, particularly where such incidents are exploited by
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">other artificially intelligent systems designed to impair or prevent the intervention of human control.</font></div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The domestic political environment, as well as political and diplomatic events within
the United States and abroad, such as the U.S. budget and deficit </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">reduction plan and foreign policy tensions with foreign nations, including embargoes, tariffs, sanctions,
trade wars, and other similar initiatives or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">developments, has resulted, and may in the future result, in a government shutdown or otherwise adversely affect the U.S.
regulatory landscape, the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">general market environment and/or investor sentiment, which could have an adverse impact on the Fund&#8217;s investments and operations. Additional
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and/or prolonged U.S. federal government shutdowns, U.S. foreign policy, the imposition of tariffs, or other U.S. economic policies and any related </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">domestic and/or geopolitical tensions may affect investor and consumer confidence and may adversely impact financial markets and the broader </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">economy, perhaps suddenly and to a significant degree. Governmental and quasi-governmental authorities and regulators throughout the world have </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">previously responded to serious economic disruptions with a variety of significant fiscal and monetary policy changes, including but not limited to, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">direct capital infusions into companies, new monetary programs and dramatically lower interest rates. An unexpected or sudden reversal of these </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">policies, or the ineffectiveness of these policies, could increase volatility in securities markets, which could adversely affect the Fund&#8217;s investments. Any </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">market disruptions could also prevent the Fund from executing advantageous investment decisions in a timely manner. Funds that have focused their </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investments on a region enduring geopolitical market disruption will face higher risks of loss, although the increasing interconnectivity between </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">global economies and financial markets can lead to events or conditions in one country, region or financial market adversely impacting a different </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">country, region or financial market. Thus, investors should closely monitor current market conditions to determine whether the Fund meets their </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">individual financial needs and tolerance for risk.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">When inflationary price movements occur, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">fixed income securities</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> markets may experience heightened levels of interest rate, volatility and liquidity </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">risk. Interest rate
increases in the future could cause the value of a fund that invests in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">fixed income securities</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> to decrease, which could force the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund to liquidate investments at disadvantageous times or prices,
therefore adversely affecting the Fund and its shareholders.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Higher interest rates generally lower the values of real estate-related assets. When this does not occur as expected, it presents an increased risk of
a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">correction or severe downturn in real estate-related asset prices, which could adversely impact the value of other investments, such as loans, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securitized debt and other fixed income securities. Such an impact could materialize in one real estate sector and not another, or in a different manner </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">in different real estate sectors. Examples of the risks faced by real estate-related assets include: tenant vacancy rates, increased tenant turnover and </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">tenant concentration; general real estate headwinds, including delinquencies and difficulties in collecting rents and other payments (which increases </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the risk of owners being unable to pay or otherwise defaulting on their own borrowings and obligations); decreases in property values; increases in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inflation, upkeep costs and other expenses; fluctuations in rents; and increased concentration in ownership of certain types of properties.</font><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Exchanges and securities markets may close early, close late or issue trading halts on specific securities or generally, which may result in, among other </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">things, the Fund being unable to buy or sell certain securities or financial instruments at an advantageous time or accurately price its portfolio </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investments. In addition, the Fund may rely on various third-party sources to calculate its NAV. As a result, the Fund is subject to certain operational </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">risks associated with reliance on service providers and service providers&#8217; data sources. In particular, errors or systems failures and other technological </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">issues may adversely impact the Fund&#8217;s calculation of its NAV, and such NAV calculation issues may result in inaccurately calculated NAVs, delays in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">NAV calculation and/or the inability to calculate NAVs over extended periods. The Fund may be unable to recover any losses associated with such </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">failures.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Issuer Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The value of a security may decline for reasons related to the issuer, such as management performance, major litigation, investigations or other </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">controversies, changes in the issuer&#8217;s financial condition or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">credit rating</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, changes in government regulations affecting the issuer or its competitive </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">environment and strategic
initiatives such as mergers, acquisitions or dispositions and the market response to any such initiatives, financial leverage, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">reputation or reduced demand for the
issuer&#8217;s goods or services, as well as the historical and prospective earnings of the issuer and the value of its </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">assets. A change in the financial condition of a
single issuer may affect one or more other issuers or securities markets as a whole. These risks can </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">apply to the Fund and to the issuers of securities and other instruments
in which the Fund invests.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Liquidity
Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Securities and Exchange Commission (the
&#8220;SEC&#8221;) defines liquidity risk as the risk that the Fund could not meet requests to redeem shares issued </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">by the Fund without significant dilution of remaining
investors&#8217; interests in the Fund. Liquidity risk exists when particular investments are difficult to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">purchase or sell. </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Illiquid investments</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> are investments that the Fund reasonably expects cannot be sold or
disposed of in current market conditions </font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:right;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">February 21, 2026&nbsp;(as supplemented March 31, 2026) |
</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">&#8194;&#8194;</font><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">9</font></div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div>
<hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_c860aaf9-7e50-4176-bbd5-2fbb95d53c49_6"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">in seven calendar days or less without the
sale or disposition significantly changing the market value of the investment. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Illiquid investments</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">become harder to value, especially in changing markets. The Fund&#8217;s investments in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">illiquid investments</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may reduce the returns of the Fund because </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">it may be unable to sell the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">illiquid investments</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> at an advantageous time or price or possibly require the Fund to dispose of other investments at </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">unfavorable
times or prices in order to satisfy its obligations, which could prevent the Fund from taking advantage of other investment opportunities. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Illiquidity can be caused by,
among other things, a drop in overall market trading volume, an inability to find a willing buyer, or legal restrictions on the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities' resale. Additionally, the market
for certain investments may become illiquid under adverse market or economic conditions independent of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">any specific adverse changes in the conditions of a particular issuer,
such as during political events (including periods of rapid interest rate changes).</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">There can be no assurance that an investment that is deemed to be liquid when purchased will continue to be liquid while it is held by the Fund </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and/or when the Fund wishes to dispose of it. Bond markets have consistently grown over the past three decades while the capacity for traditional </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">dealer counterparties to engage in fixed income trading has not kept pace and in some cases has decreased. As a result, dealer inventories of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">corporate bonds, which provide a core indication of the ability of financial intermediaries to &#8220;make markets,&#8221; are at or near historic lows in relation to </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">market size. Because market makers seek to provide stability to a market through their intermediary services, the significant reduction in dealer </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">inventories could potentially lead to decreased liquidity and increased volatility in the fixed income markets. Such issues may be exacerbated during </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">periods of economic uncertainty.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">In such cases, the Fund, due to regulatory limitations on investments in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">illiquid
investments</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> and the difficulty in purchasing and selling such </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities or instruments, may be
unable to achieve its desired level of exposure to a certain sector. To the extent that the Fund&#8217;s principal investment </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">strategies involve securities of companies with
smaller market capitalizations, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.) securities</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, Rule 144A
securities, Regulation S </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities, illiquid sectors of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">fixed income
securities</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> or securities with substantial market and/or credit risk, the Fund will tend to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">have the greatest exposure to
liquidity risk. Further, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">fixed income securities</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> with longer </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">durations</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> until maturity face heightened levels of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">liquidity risk as compared to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">fixed income securities</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> with shorter </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">durations</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> until maturity. Finally, liquidity risk refers to the risk of unusually high </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">redemption requests, redemption
requests by certain large shareholders such as institutional investors or asset allocators, or other unusual market </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">conditions that may make it difficult for the Fund to
sell investments within the allowable time period to meet redemptions. Meeting such redemption </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">requests could require the Fund to sell securities at reduced prices or under
unfavorable conditions, which would have an adverse effect on the Fund. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">It may also be the case that other market participants may be attempting to liquidate fixed income
holdings at the same time as the Fund, causing </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">increased supply in the market and contributing to liquidity risk and downward pricing pressure.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The action(s) of governments and regulators may have the effect of reducing market
liquidity, market resiliency and money supply. Certain accounts </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or PIMCO affiliates may from time to time own (beneficially or of record) or control a significant percentage
of the Fund's shares. Redemptions by </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">these shareholders of their holdings in the Fund may impact the Fund's NAV and the market price and secondary market liquidity of Fund
shares. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">These redemptions may also force the Fund to sell its securities, which may negatively impact the Fund's brokerage costs.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Liquidity risk also refers to the risk that the Fund may be required to hold
additional cash or sell other investments in order to obtain cash to close out </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> or meet the liquidity demands that </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> can create to make payments of margin, collateral, or settlement payments to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">counterparties. The Fund may
have to sell a security at a disadvantageous time or price to meet such obligations.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Derivatives Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> and other similar instruments (referred to collectively as &#8220;</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">&#8221;) are financial contracts whose value depends on, or is derived </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">from, the value of an underlying asset, reference rate or index. The various
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> instruments that the Fund may use are referenced under </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">&#8220;Characteristics and Risks of Securities and Investment Techniques&#8212;Derivatives&#8221; in this prospectus and described in more detail under &#8220;Investment </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Objectives and Policies&#8221; in the SAI. The Fund may use </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> as a substitute for taking a position in the underlying asset, as part of strategies </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">designed to gain
exposure to, for example, issuers, portions of the yield curve, indexes, sectors, currencies and/or geographic regions, and/or to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">manage (which may mean either to increase
or decrease) exposure to other risks, such as interest rate, credit or currency risk. The Fund may also use </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> for leverage, in which case their use would involve leveraging risk, and in some cases, may subject the Fund to the potential for </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">unlimited loss. The use of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> or other similar instruments may cause the Fund&#8217;s investment returns to be impacted by the performance of
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">assets the Fund does not own, potentially resulting in the Fund&#8217;s total investment exposure exceeding the value of its portfolio.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Investments in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may take the form of buying and/or writing (selling) </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, and/or the Fund may otherwise become an obligor </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">under a
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> transaction. These transactions may produce short-term capital gains
in the form of premiums or other returns for the Fund </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">(which may support, constitute and/or increase the distributions paid by, or the yield of, the Fund) but create the
risk of losses that can significantly </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exceed such current income or other returns. For example, the premium received for writing a call option may be dwarfed by the losses
the Fund may </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">incur if the call option is exercised, and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> transactions where the Fund is an obligor can produce an up-front benefit, but the potential for </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">leveraged
losses. The distributions, or distribution rate, paid by the Fund should not be viewed as the total returns or overall performance of the Fund. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">These strategies may also
produce adverse tax consequences (for example, the Fund's income and gain-generating strategies may generate current </font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">10&#8194;&#8194;Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;"> | PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div> <hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_c860aaf9-7e50-4176-bbd5-2fbb95d53c49_7"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">Prospectus</font></div>
</div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">income and gains taxable as ordinary
income) and limit the Fund's opportunity to profit or otherwise benefit from certain gains. The Fund may enter </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">into opposing </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> transactions, or otherwise take opposing positions. Such transactions can generate
distributable gains (which, as noted </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">elsewhere, may be taxed as ordinary income) and create the risk of losses and NAV declines.</font></div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund&#8217;s use of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> instruments involves risks different from, and possibly greater than, the risks
associated with investing directly in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities and other traditional investments. </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may increase market exposure and are subject to a number of risks, such as
liquidity risk </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">(which may be heightened for highly-customized </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">), interest rate risk, market risk, leverage risk, counterparty (including credit) risk, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">operational risk
(such as documentation issues, settlement issues and systems failures), legal risk (such as insufficient documentation, insufficient </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">capacity or authority of a counterparty,
and issues with the legality or enforceability of a contract), management risk, risks arising from changes in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">applicable regulatory requirements, risks arising from margin
requirements, risks arising from mispricing or valuation complexity (including the risk of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">improper valuation), governmental risk, risks associated with the underlying
asset, reference rate or index, and risks associated with sanctions. They </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">also involve the risk that changes in the value of a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> instrument may not correlate perfectly with the underlying asset, rate or index.
By </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investing in a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> instrument, the Fund could lose more than the initial amount invested and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may increase the volatility of the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund, especially in unusual or extreme market conditions. Certain </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> have the potential for unlimited loss, regardless of the size of the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">initial investment. The Fund may utilize asset segregation and posting of collateral for risk management or other purposes. The Fund may be required </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">to hold additional cash or sell other investments in order to obtain cash to close out a position and changes in the value of a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may also
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">create margin delivery or settlement payment obligations for the Fund. Also, suitable </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> transactions may not be available in all </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">circumstances and there can be no assurance that the Fund will engage in these transactions to reduce exposure to other risks when that would be </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">beneficial or that, if used, such strategies will be successful. In addition, the Fund&#8217;s use of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may increase or accelerate the amount of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">taxes payable by shareholders. Non-centrally-cleared over-the-counter (&#8220;OTC&#8221;)
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> are also subject to the risk that a counterparty to the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">transaction will not fulfill its contractual obligations to the other party, as many of the protections afforded to centrally-cleared </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">transactions might not be available for non-centrally-cleared OTC </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">. The primary credit risk on </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> or other similar investments </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">that are exchange-traded or traded through a central clearing counterparty
resides with the Fund&#8217;s clearing broker or the clearinghouse.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> that are cleared by a central clearing organization can still be subject to
different risks, including the creditworthiness of the central </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">clearing organization and its members.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">In addition, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> that are traded on an exchange are subject to the risk that an exchange may limit
the maximum daily price fluctuation of a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> contract and restrict or
suspend trading of a contract that has reached a limit. Such limit governs only price movements of a contract </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">during a particular trading day and therefore does not limit
potential losses because the limit may work to prevent the liquidation of unfavorable </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">positions. A daily limit may be reached for several consecutive days with little or no
trading.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Participation in the markets for </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> instruments involves investment risks and transaction costs to which the Fund may
not be subject absent </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the use of these strategies. The skills needed to successfully execute </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> strategies may be different from those needed for other types of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">transactions. If the Fund incorrectly forecasts the value and/or creditworthiness of securities, currencies, interest rates, counterparties or other </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">economic factors involved in a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> transaction, the Fund might have been in a better position if the Fund had not entered into such </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> transaction. In evaluating the risks and contractual obligations associated with
particular </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> instruments or other similar </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investments, it is important to consider that certain </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> transactions, absent a default or termination event, may only be modified or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">terminated by mutual consent of
the Fund and its counterparty. Therefore, it may not be possible for the Fund to modify, terminate, or offset the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund&#8217;s obligations or the Fund&#8217;s exposure to
the risks associated with a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> transaction prior to its scheduled
termination or maturity date, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">which may create a possibility of increased volatility and/or decreased liquidity to the Fund. In such cases, the Fund may experience
losses.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Because the markets for certain </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> instruments (including markets located in foreign countries) are relatively new
and still developing, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">appropriate </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> transactions may not be available in all circumstances for risk management or other purposes. Upon the expiration of a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">particular contract, the Fund may wish to retain its position in the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> instrument by entering into a similar contract, but may be unable to do </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">so if the counterparty to the
original contract is unwilling to enter into the new contract and no other appropriate counterparty can be found. When </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">such markets are unavailable, the Fund will be subject
to increased liquidity and investment risk.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">When a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> is used as a hedge against a position that the Fund holds, any loss generated by
the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> generally should be </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">substantially offset by gains on the hedged investment, and vice versa. Although hedging can reduce or eliminate losses, it can also reduce or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">eliminate gains. Hedges are sometimes subject to imperfect matching between the
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> and the underlying instrument, and there can be no </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">assurance that the Fund&#8217;s hedging transactions will be effective. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Derivatives</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> used for hedging or risk management may not operate as intended or </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">may expose the Fund to additional risks.
In addition, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> used for hedging may partially protect the Fund from
the risks they were intended </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">to hedge yet not fully mitigate the impact of such risks.</font></div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:right;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">February 21, 2026&nbsp;(as supplemented March 31, 2026) |
</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">&#8194;&#8194;</font><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">11</font></div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div>
<hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_c860aaf9-7e50-4176-bbd5-2fbb95d53c49_8"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The regulation of the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> markets has increased over time, and additional future regulation of the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> markets may make </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> more costly, may limit the availability or reduce the liquidity of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, or may otherwise adversely affect the value or performance </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">of </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">.
Any such adverse future developments could impair the effectiveness or raise the costs of the Fund&#8217;s </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> transactions, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">impede the employment of the Fund&#8217;s </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> strategies, or adversely affect the Fund&#8217;s performance and cause the Fund
to lose value.</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Exchange-Traded Fund
(&#8220;ETF&#8221;) Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Investments in ETFs entail certain risks.
In the case of actively managed ETFs, there is a risk that the ETF may not achieve its investment objective. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Investments in ETFs designed to track an index involve the risk
that the ETF&#8217;s performance may not track the performance of the index the ETF is </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">designed to track. This deviation may occur due to cash inflows and outflows from and
to investors buying and redeeming shares or due to occasional </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">differences between the composition of the index and the securities held by the ETF. In addition, investments
in ETFs involve the risk that the market </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">prices of ETF shares will fluctuate, sometimes rapidly and materially, in response to changes in the ETF&#8217;s NAV, the value of
ETF holdings and supply </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and demand for ETF shares. Although ETFs will generally trade close to NAV, market volatility, lack of an active trading market for ETF shares,
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">disruptions at market participants (such as authorized participants or market makers) and any disruptions in the ordinary functioning of the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">creation/redemption process may result in ETF shares trading significantly above (at a &#8220;premium&#8221;) or below (at a &#8220;discount&#8221;) NAV. Significant losses </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">may result when transacting in ETF shares in these and other circumstances.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Foreign (Non-U.S.) Investment Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Foreign (non-U.S.) securities</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">&nbsp;may experience more
rapid and extreme changes in value than securities of U.S. issuers or securities that trade </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exclusively in U.S. markets. The securities markets of many </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.)</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> countries are relatively small and less developed, with a limited </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">number of companies representing a small number of industries. Additionally, issuers of
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.) securities</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> are usually not subject to the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">same degree of regulation as U.S. issuers. Financial reporting, legal, corporate governance, accounting and auditing standards of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.)</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">countries differ, in some cases significantly, from U.S. standards. Global economies and financial markets are becoming increasingly interconnected, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and conditions and events in one country, region or financial market may adversely impact issuers in a different country, region or financial market. </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Foreign (non-U.S.) </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">market trading hours, clearance and settlement procedures, and holiday
schedules may limit the Fund&#8217;s ability to buy and sell </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities. Investments in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.)</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> markets may also be adversely affected by governmental actions such as the
imposition of capital </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">controls, nationalization of companies or industries, expropriation of assets or the imposition of punitive taxes. The governments of certain countries
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">may prohibit or impose substantial restrictions on foreign investing in their capital markets or in certain sectors or industries. In addition, a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">(non-U.S.)</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> government may limit or cause delay in the convertibility or repatriation of its currency which would adversely affect the U.S. dollar value </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and/or liquidity of investments denominated in that currency. Certain </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign
(non-U.S.)</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> investments may become less liquid in response to market </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">developments or adverse
investor perceptions, or become illiquid after purchase by the Fund, particularly during periods of market turmoil and may </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">render holdings in that </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.)</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> country illiquid or even worthless. A reduction in trading in securities
of issuers located in countries whose </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">economies are heavily dependent upon trading with key partners may have an adverse impact on the Fund&#8217;s investments.
Additionally, events and </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">evolving conditions in certain markets or regions may alter the risk profile of investments tied to those markets or regions. This may cause
investments </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">tied to such markets or regions to become riskier or more volatile, even when investments in such markets or regions were perceived as comparatively </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">stable historically.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Also, nationalization, expropriation or confiscatory taxation, unstable governments, decreased market liquidity, currency blockage, market disruptions, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">political changes, security suspensions, diplomatic developments, trade restrictions (including tariffs) or the imposition of sanctions or other similar </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">measures could adversely affect the Fund&#8217;s investments in a </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.)</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> country and may render holdings in that </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.)</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">country illiquid or even worthless. In the event of nationalization, expropriation or other
confiscation, the Fund could lose its entire investment in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.) securities</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">. The type and severity of sanctions and other similar measures, including counter sanctions and other retaliatory </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">actions, that may be imposed could vary broadly in scope, and their impact is difficult to ascertain. These types of measures may include, but are not </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">limited to, banning a sanctioned country or certain persons or entities associated with such country from global payment systems that facilitate </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">cross-border payments, restricting securities transactions, restricting dealings with entities that are critical to the infrastructure of securities and </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">related transactions in specific jurisdictions, restricting transactions in specified sectors of certain countries, and freezing the assets of particular </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">countries, entities or persons. The imposition of sanctions and other similar measures could impact the Fund's portfolio holdings by, among other </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">things, reducing their value and/or liquidity or causing a downgrade in credit ratings. In addition, these measures could result in currency devaluation </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or volatility, increased market volatility, and/or economic disruptions in the sanctioned country or throughout the world. Sanctions and other similar </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">measures could directly or indirectly limit or prevent the Fund from buying and selling securities, receiving interest or principal payments due on the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities, significantly delay or prevent the settlement of securities transactions and adversely impact the Fund's liquidity and performance and/or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">prevent the liquidation of the Fund holding sanctioned securities. The U.S. government may renegotiate some of its global trade relationships with </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">foreign governments and may impose or threaten to impose significant tariffs. The imposition of tariffs, trade restrictions, currency restrictions or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">similar actions (or retaliatory measures taken in response to such actions) could contribute to volatility or overall declines in the U.S. and global </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investment markets. Adverse conditions in a certain region can adversely affect securities of other countries whose economies appear to be unrelated. </font></div> </div> </div>
<div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">12&#8194;&#8194;Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;"> | PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div> <hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_c860aaf9-7e50-4176-bbd5-2fbb95d53c49_9"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">Prospectus</font></div>
</div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">To the extent that the Fund invests a
significant portion of its assets in a specific geographic region or in securities denominated in a particular </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.)</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> currency, the Fund will generally have more exposure to regional economic risks, including weather emergencies and natural </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">disasters, associated with </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.)</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> investments. </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Foreign (non-U.S.) securities</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may also be less liquid (particularly during market </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">closures due to local holidays or other reasons) and more
difficult to value than securities of U.S. issuers.</font></div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Sovereign Debt Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Sovereign debt risk is the risk that </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">fixed income
instruments</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> issued by sovereign entities may decline in value as a result of default or other
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">adverse credit events resulting from an issuer&#8217;s inability or unwillingness to make principal or interest payments in a timely fashion. A sovereign </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">entity&#8217;s failure to make timely payments on its debt can result from many factors, including, without limitation, insufficient </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.) </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">currency</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> reserves or an inability to sufficiently manage fluctuations in relative currency valuations, an inability or unwillingness to satisfy the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">demands of creditors and/or relevant supranational entities regarding debt service or economic reforms, the size of the debt burden relative to </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">economic output and tax revenues, cash flow difficulties, and other political and social considerations. The risk of loss to the Fund in the event of a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">sovereign debt default or other adverse credit event is heightened by the unlikelihood of any formal recourse or means to enforce its rights as a </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">holder of the sovereign debt. In addition, sovereign debt restructurings, which may be shaped by entities and factors beyond the Fund&#8217;s control, may </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">result in a loss in value of the Fund&#8217;s sovereign debt holdings.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Currency Risk</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">If the Fund invests directly in </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.) currencies</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> or in securities that trade in, and receive revenues in, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.)
currencies</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or other instruments that provide exposure to </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.) currencies</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, it will be subject to the risk that those currencies </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">will decline in value relative to the U.S. dollar, or, in the case of hedging positions, that the U.S. dollar will decline in value relative to the currency </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">being hedged. Although the Fund may attempt to hedge its currency exposure into the U.S. dollar, it may not be successful in reducing the effects of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">currency fluctuations. The Fund may also hedge from one foreign currency to another. In addition, the Fund&#8217;s use of currency hedging may not be </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">successful and the use of such strategies may lower the Fund&#8217;s potential returns.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;">
<div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Currency rates in foreign (non-U.S.) countries may fluctuate significantly over short periods of time for a number of reasons, including due to changes
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">in interest or inflation rates, balance of payments and governmental surpluses or deficits, intervention (or the failure to intervene) by U.S. or foreign </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">(non-U.S.) governments, central banks or supranational entities such as the International Monetary Fund, the imposition of currency controls or other </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">political developments in the U.S. or abroad. As a result, the Fund&#8217;s investments in or exposure to </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.) currencies</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> and/or foreign </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">(non-U.S.) currency-denominated securities may reduce the returns of the Fund. Devaluation of a currency by a country&#8217;s government or banking </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">authority can significantly impact the value of any investments denominated in that currency. The Fund may also be adversely impacted by expenses </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">incurred by converting between currencies to purchase and sell securities not valued in the U.S. dollar, as well as by currency restrictions, exchange </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">control regulation, or governmental restrictions that limit or otherwise delay the Fund&#8217;s ability to convert currencies.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Currency risk may be particularly high to the extent that the Fund invests in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.) currencies</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> or engages in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign currency </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">transactions</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> that are economically tied to emerging market countries. These currency transactions may present market, credit, currency, liquidity, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">legal, political and other risks different from, or greater than, the risks of investing in developed </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign (non-U.S.) currencies</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> or engaging in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">foreign currency transactions</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> that are economically tied to developed foreign
countries.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Leveraging Risk</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Certain transactions may give rise to a form of leverage. Such transactions may
include, among others, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">reverse repurchase agreements, loans of
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">portfolio securities,</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> and the use of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">when-issued, delayed delivery or forward commitment transactions</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">. The use of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivatives</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">also create leveraging risk. The Fund also may be exposed to leveraging risk by
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">borrowing</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> money for investment purposes. Leverage may cause the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund to liquidate portfolio positions to satisfy its obligations when it may not be advantageous to do so. Leverage, including </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">borrowing</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">, may cause </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">the Fund to be more volatile than if the Fund had not been leveraged. This is because leverage tends to exaggerate the effect of any increase or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">decrease in the value of the Fund's portfolio securities. The use of leverage may also increase the Fund's sensitivity to interest rate risks. Certain types </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">of leveraging transactions, such as </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">short sales</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> that are not &#8220;against the box&#8221;&nbsp;(i.e., short sales where the Fund does not hold the security or have the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">right to acquire it without payment of further consideration), could theoretically be subject to unlimited losses in cases where the Fund, for any </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">reason, is unable to close out the transaction. In addition, to the extent the Fund borrows money, interest costs on such </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">borrowings</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> may not be </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">recovered by any appreciation of the securities purchased with the borrowed amounts and could exceed the Fund&#8217;s investment returns, resulting in </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">greater losses. Moreover, to make payments of interest and other loan costs, the Fund may be forced to sell portfolio securities when it is not </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">otherwise advantageous to do so. When the Fund reduces or discontinues its use of leverage (&#8220;deleveraging&#8221;), it may be required to sell portfolio </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">securities at inopportune times to repay leverage obligations, which could result in realized losses and a decrease in the Fund's net asset value. </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Deleveraging involves complex operational processes, including the coordination of asset sales, repayment of debt, and potential restructuring of the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Fund's capital and may involve significant costs, including transaction costs associated with the sale of portfolio securities and prepayment penalties </font></div> </div> </div>
<div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:right;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">February 21, 2026&nbsp;(as supplemented March 31, 2026) |
</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;">&#8194;&#8194;</font><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">13</font></div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div>
<hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_c860aaf9-7e50-4176-bbd5-2fbb95d53c49_10"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">on borrowed funds. Leveraging transactions
pursued by the Fund may increase its </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">duration</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> and sensitivity to interest rate
changes and other market </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">risks. The Fund may continue to use leverage even if available financing rates are higher than anticipated returns, including, for example, in cases
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">where deleveraging, including any expenses related thereto, might be viewed as detrimental to the Fund&#8217;s portfolio.</font></div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Management Risk</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund is subject to management risk because they are an actively managed investment
portfolio. PIMCO and each individual portfolio manager </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">will apply investment techniques and risk analysis and will, in some cases, rely partially or entirely upon or be
informed by one or more quantitative </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">models in making investment decisions for the Fund. PIMCO and each portfolio manager may not consider every factor or may determine that
certain </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">factors are more significant than others. There can be no guarantee that these decisions will produce the desired results or that the due diligence </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">conducted by PIMCO and individual portfolio managers will evaluate every factor prior to investing in a company or issuer and expose all material </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">risks associated with an investment. Additionally, PIMCO and individual portfolio managers may not be able to identify suitable investment </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">opportunities and may face competition from other investment managers when identifying and consummating certain investments. Certain securities </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or other instruments in which the Fund seeks to invest may not be available in the quantities desired, including in circumstances where other funds </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">for which PIMCO acts as investment adviser, including funds with names, investment objectives and policies, and/or portfolio management teams, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">similar to the Fund, are seeking to invest in the same or similar securities or instruments. In addition, regulatory restrictions, actual or potential </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">conflicts of interest or other considerations may cause PIMCO to restrict or prohibit participation in certain investments. In such circumstances, PIMCO </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or the individual portfolio managers may determine to purchase other securities or instruments as substitutes. Such substitute securities or </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">instruments may not perform as intended, which could result in losses to the Fund. To the extent the Fund employs strategies targeting perceived </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">pricing inefficiencies, arbitrage strategies or similar strategies, it is subject to the risk that the pricing or valuation of the securities and instruments </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">involved in such strategies may change unexpectedly, which may result in reduced returns or losses to the Fund. The Fund is also subject to the risk </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">that deficiencies in the internal systems or controls of PIMCO or another service provider will cause losses for the Fund or hinder Fund operations. For </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">example, trading delays or errors (both human and systemic) could prevent the Fund from purchasing a security expected to appreciate in value. </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Please refer to &#8220;Portfolio Managers &#8211; Conflicts of Interest&#8221; in the SAI for further information. Additionally, actual or potential conflicts of interest, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">legislative, regulatory, or tax restrictions, policies or developments may affect the investment techniques available to PIMCO and each individual </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">portfolio manager in connection with managing the Fund may cause PIMCO to restrict or prohibit participation in certain investments and may also </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">adversely affect the ability of the Fund to achieve its investment objective. There also can be no assurance that all of the personnel of PIMCO will </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">continue to be associated with PIMCO for any length of time. The loss of services of one or more key employees of PIMCO could have an adverse </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">impact on the Fund&#8217;s ability to realize its investment objective.</font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Short Exposure Risk</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund&#8217;s </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">short sales </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and short positions, if any, are subject to special risks. A </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">short sale</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> involves the sale by the Fund of a security that it does not </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">own with the hope of purchasing the same security at a later date at a lower price. The Fund may also enter into a short position through a forward </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">commitment or a short </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> position through a futures contract or swap agreement. If the price of the security or
</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">derivative</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> has increased </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">during this time, then the Fund will incur a loss equal to the increase in price from the time that the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">short sale</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> was entered into plus any transaction </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">costs (</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;">i.e.</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">,
premiums and interest) paid to the broker-dealer to borrow securities. Therefore, </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">short sales</font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> involve the risk that losses may be </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exaggerated, potentially losing more money than the actual cost of the
investment. By contrast, a loss on a long position arises from decreases in the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">value of the security and is limited by the fact that a security&#8217;s value cannot
decrease below zero.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">By investing the proceeds received from
selling securities short, the Fund could be deemed to be employing a form of leverage, which creates special </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">risks. The use of leverage may increase the Fund&#8217;s
exposure to long security positions and make any change in the Fund&#8217;s NAV greater than it would </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">be without the use of leverage. This could result in increased
volatility of returns. There is no guarantee that any leveraging strategy the Fund employs </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">will be successful during any period in which it is employed.</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">In times of unusual or adverse market, economic, regulatory, environmental or
political conditions, the Fund may not be able, fully or partially, to </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">implement its short selling strategy. Periods of unusual or adverse market, economic, regulatory,
environmental or political conditions generally may </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">exist for as long as six months and, in some cases, much longer. In response to market events, the SEC and regulatory
authorities in other jurisdictions </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">may adopt (and in certain cases, have adopted) bans on, and/or reporting requirements for, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">short sales</font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;"> of certain securities, including short positions </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">on such securities acquired through swaps. Restrictions on and/or reporting requirements applicable to short selling and short positions may </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">negatively impact and materially impair the Fund's ability to execute certain transactions. Also, there is the risk that the third party to the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">short sale </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">or short position will not fulfill its contractual obligations, causing a loss to
the Fund.</font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Disclosure of Portfolio Holdings</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:2pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Please see &#8220;Disclosure of Portfolio Holdings&#8221; in the SAI for information about the availability of the complete schedule of the Fund&#8217;s holdings.</font></div> </div>
</div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:0.53pt;text-align:left;top:8.73pt;width:538pt;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;line-height:14.21pt;">14&#8194;&#8194;Prospectus</font><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:8pt;line-height:14.21pt;"> | PIMCO ETF
Trust</font></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-bottom:5.0pt;width:100%;"> </div> <hr style="clear:both;margin-bottom:0.25pt;margin-left:0.25pt;margin-right:0.25pt;margin-top:40.0pt;">
</div> <div> <div><a name="xx_163e316f-87a5-47d6-8e10-fbe026c592ba_1"></A> <div style="page-break-after:always;position:relative;"> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:34pt;width:538pt;min-height:72pt;"> <div style="line-height:19.0pt;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:19pt;line-height:19pt;">Prospectus</font></div>
</div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-70pt;width:538pt;min-height:51.8pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:left;">
<hr style="background-color:#333333;height:0.5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0%;margin-top:42.33pt;position:relative;text-align:left;top:6.73pt;width:538pt;"> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div>
<div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:-16pt;width:538pt;min-height:642pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Management of the
Fund</font></div> <div style="line-height:14.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;">Investment Manager</font></div> </div>
<div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:2pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:2pt;"><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">PIMCO serves as the investment manager for the Fund. Subject to the supervision of the
Board of Trustees, PIMCO is responsible for managing the </font><font style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investment activities of the Fund and the Fund's business affairs and other administrative matters.</font><font
style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;line-height:12pt;"> </font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">PIMCO is located at 650 Newport Center Drive, Newport Beach, CA 92660. Organized in 1971, PIMCO provides investment management and </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">advisory services to private accounts of institutional and individual clients and to mutual funds. As of December 31, 2025, PIMCO had approximately </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">$2.26 trillion in assets under management, including $1.84 trillion in third-party client assets. Assets include $81.0 billion (as of September 30, 2025) </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">in assets managed by Prime Real Estate (formerly Allianz Real Estate), an affiliate and wholly-owned subsidiary of PIMCO and PIMCO Europe GmbH, </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">that includes PIMCO Prime Real Estate GmbH, PIMCO Prime Real Estate LLC and their subsidiaries and affiliates. PIMCO Prime Real Estate LLC </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">investment professionals provide investment management and other services as dual personnel through Pacific Investment Management Company </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">LLC. PIMCO Prime Real Estate GmbH operates separately from PIMCO.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Management Fees</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The Fund pays for the advisory and supervisory and administrative services it requires under what is essentially an all-in fee structure. The Fund pays </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">monthly Management Fees to PIMCO at the following annual rate (stated as a percentage of the average daily net assets of the Fund&nbsp;taken </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">separately) of 0.25%.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">In addition to providing investment advisory services, PIMCO provides or procures supervisory and administrative services for shareholders and also </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">bears the costs of various third-party services required by the Fund, including audit, custodial, portfolio accounting, legal, transfer agency and printing </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">costs. The Fund bears other expenses which are not covered under the management fee which may vary and affect the total level of expenses paid by </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">shareholders, such as taxes and governmental fees, brokerage fees, commissions and other transaction expenses (including, without limitation, fees </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and expenses of outside legal counsel or third-party consultants retained in connection with reviewing, negotiating and structuring specialized loans </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and other investments made by the Fund, and any costs associated with originating loans, asset securitizations, alternative lending-related strategies </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and so-called &#8220;broken-deal costs&#8221; (e.g., fees, costs, expenses and liabilities, including, for example, due diligence-related fees, costs, expenses and </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">liabilities, with respect to unconsummated investments)), organizational and offering expenses of the Trust and the Fund, and any other expenses </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">which are capitalized in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles, costs of borrowing money, including interest expenses, securities </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">lending expenses, extraordinary expenses (such as litigation and indemnification expenses) and fees and expenses of the Trust&#8217;s Independent Trustees </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">and their counsel. PIMCO generally earns a profit on the management fee paid by the Fund. Also, under the terms of the investment management </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">agreement, PIMCO, and not Fund shareholders, would benefit from any price decreases in third-party services, including decreases resulting from an </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">increase in net assets.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">A discussion regarding the basis for the Board of Trustees&#8217; approval of the Fund&#8217;s investment management agreement will be&nbsp;available in the Fund's </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">report filed on Form N-CSR.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Expense Limitation Agreement</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">PIMCO has contractually agreed, through October 31, 2027, to waive a portion of the Fund&#8217;s Management Fee, or reimburse the Fund, to the extent </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">that the Fund&#8217;s organizational expenses, pro rata share of expenses related to obtaining or maintaining a Legal Entity Identifier and pro rata share of </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Trustee fees exceed 0.0049% (the &#8220;Expense Limit&#8221;) (calculated as a percentage of the Fund&#8217;s average daily net assets). The Expense Limitation </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Agreement will automatically renew for one-year terms unless PIMCO provides written notice to the Trust at least 30 days prior to the end of the then </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">current term. In any month in which the investment management agreement is in effect, PIMCO is entitled to reimbursement by the Fund of any </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">portion of the Management Fee waived or reimbursed as set forth above (the &#8220;Reimbursement Amount&#8221;) within thirty-six months of the time of the </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">waiver, provided that such amount paid to PIMCO will not: 1) together with any organizational expenses, pro rata share of expenses related to </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">obtaining or maintaining a Legal Entity Identifier and pro rata Trustee fees, exceed, for such month, the Expense Limit (or the amount of the expense </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">limit in place at the time the amount being recouped was originally waived if lower than the Expense Limit); 2) exceed the total Reimbursement </font><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">Amount; or 3) include any amounts previously reimbursed to PIMCO.</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:10pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:10pt;"><font
style="color:#00687D;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;">Individual Portfolio Managers</font></div> </div> <div style="line-height:12.0pt;margin-top:4pt;text-align:left;"> <div style="margin-top:4pt;"><font
style="color:#333333;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:10pt;">The following individuals have or share primary responsibility for managing the Fund.</font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:1pt;">&#8195;</font></div>
</div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"> </div> <div style="float:left;margin-left:30pt;margin-top:12pt;width:538pt;min-height:12pt;"> <div style="line-height:14.21pt;text-align:right;">
